-- title:
--   d = dP n is the integer 2^75-th root of b (κ = 2⁻¹²⁹ constants)
-- statement:
--   **d = dP n is the integer 2^75-th root of b**, at the `same-network-129` constants.
--
--   This is `NLogN.KFM.dP_spec` from xuanji's $\kappa = 2^{-182}$ formalization (statement and proof unchanged apart from the constants) with the constants of §8 replaced by those of the community patch `same-network-129`: $\tau = 1 - 2^{-42}$ (same swap networks, motif exponent from $\log 10^6 < 14$), $\varepsilon = c = 2^{-43}$, $\lambda' = 1 - 2^{-85}$ ($\delta = 1/16$ unchanged). The parameter map $d = \lfloor b^{\varepsilon} \rfloor$, $K = \lfloor d^{c} \rfloor$, $\ell = \lceil L/d \rceil$, $\alpha = \lceil (12 d^2 b)^{1/4} \rceil$, $r = 2^{\ell}$ is the one of `Def_IntMul_OpenAI_R129`, and every constant-dependent name lives under `IntMul.OpenAI.R129.P`.
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFM 14: the setup arithmetic (§9.2), in the integer form the machine computes*.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Integer multiplication below n log n (preprint, 23 Sep 2026), https://github.com/openai/math/tree/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Integer-multiplication-below-n-log-n-September-23-2026, §8 and §9 with the same-network-129 constants of https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds. Port of `NLogN.KFM.dP_spec` (https://prove2.me/theorems/69c2f0c5-9103-4aa6-b27d-dd63371c7b0f).

